WEBVTT

00:00:21.957 --> 00:00:23.223
Dad. Sam.

00:00:23.257 --> 00:00:24.857
This is bigger than you
think. They're everywhere.

00:00:24.891 --> 00:00:26.824
Sam: if this demon killed mom
and jess and dad's closing in,

00:00:26.857 --> 00:00:28.024
We got to help.

00:00:28.058 --> 00:00:29.590
Dad doesn't want our help.

00:00:29.624 --> 00:00:32.957
I'm talking one week here, man,
to get answers, to get revenge.

00:00:32.991 --> 00:00:34.223
You think i didn't respect dad.

00:00:34.257 --> 00:00:35.891
Sorry i brought it up. I respected him.

00:00:35.924 --> 00:00:37.891
No matter what i did,
it was never good enough.

00:00:37.924 --> 00:00:39.590
So what are you saying? That
dad was disappointed in you?

00:00:39.624 --> 00:00:41.257
When we finally do find dad,

00:00:41.290 --> 00:00:44.091
I don't know if he's
even gonna want to see me.

00:00:44.124 --> 00:00:45.924
Hey! Dad.

00:00:45.957 --> 00:00:47.091
Hey, boys.

00:00:47.124 --> 00:00:49.290
Hi, sam. Hi, dad.

00:00:49.323 --> 00:00:51.924
Last time we were together,
we had one hell of a fight.

00:00:51.957 --> 00:00:54.424
Yes, sir. It's good to see you again.

00:00:54.457 --> 00:00:56.357
It's been a long time.

00:00:56.390 --> 00:00:57.390
Sam!

00:00:57.424 --> 00:00:58.724
Dean: we almost got dad killed.

00:00:58.757 --> 00:01:00.290
They're not gonna stop.
They're gonna try again.

00:01:00.323 --> 00:01:02.024
They're gonna use us to get to him.

00:01:02.058 --> 00:01:03.791
Dad's vulnerable when he's with us.

00:01:03.824 --> 00:01:05.290
I got to be a part of this fight.

00:01:05.323 --> 00:01:06.924
Sammy, this fight is just starting.

00:01:06.957 --> 00:01:09.024
You got to let me go.

00:01:29.357 --> 00:01:30.891
Beth: mr. Elkins?

00:01:33.457 --> 00:01:34.624
Mr. Elkins.

00:01:34.657 --> 00:01:36.724
Would you like another?

00:01:36.757 --> 00:01:39.390
Yeah. Thanks, beth.

00:01:42.323 --> 00:01:44.657
I thought they caught the unabomber.

00:01:44.691 --> 00:01:47.891
Yeah, poor mr. Elkins lives
all alone up in the canyon.

00:01:47.924 --> 00:01:50.657
Same seat every day,

00:01:50.691 --> 00:01:52.957
Going through his papers,
making his little notes.

00:01:52.991 --> 00:01:56.257
He's a nice old man. He's just a nut.

00:01:58.924 --> 00:02:00.457
Here you go.

00:02:26.091 --> 00:02:27.357
What'll you have?

00:02:27.390 --> 00:02:29.824
Jack all around. Leave the bottle.

00:02:29.857 --> 00:02:32.490
You hungry? We have dinner plans.

00:02:36.691 --> 00:02:39.158
Can i get you something
else, mr. Elkins?

00:03:26.857 --> 00:03:28.991
It's been a while.

00:03:29.024 --> 00:03:31.091
I got to say, you look old.

00:03:31.124 --> 00:03:33.424
What do you want? What do you think?

00:03:35.590 --> 00:03:36.924
Damn.

00:03:41.457 --> 00:03:42.724
You can do better than that.

00:03:53.991 --> 00:03:55.524
Come on, come on.

00:04:37.757 --> 00:04:39.091
Nice gun.

00:04:41.190 --> 00:04:43.857
Wouldn't do you much good, of course.

00:04:43.891 --> 00:04:46.390
Boys...

00:04:46.424 --> 00:04:48.824
We're eating in tonight.

00:05:09.091 --> 00:05:11.657
All right, dude, not a decent
lead in all of nebraska.

00:05:11.691 --> 00:05:12.891
What do you got?

00:05:12.924 --> 00:05:15.857
Well, i been scanning wyoming,
colorado, south dakota.

00:05:15.891 --> 00:05:18.991
Here
- A woman in iowa fell 10,000 feet from an airplane

00:05:19.024 --> 00:05:20.757
And survived.

00:05:20.791 --> 00:05:22.557
Sounds more like "that's incredible!"

00:05:22.590 --> 00:05:24.158
Than "the twilight zone."

00:05:24.190 --> 00:05:25.390
Yeah.

00:05:25.424 --> 00:05:28.323
Hey, you know, we could
just keep heading east -

00:05:28.357 --> 00:05:30.557
New york, upstate.

00:05:30.590 --> 00:05:32.924
Could stop by and see sarah again. Huh?

00:05:32.957 --> 00:05:35.524
She's a cool chick, man. Smokin'.

00:05:35.557 --> 00:05:39.058
You two seemed pretty
friendly. What do you say?

00:05:39.091 --> 00:05:41.058
Yeah, i don't know. Maybe someday.

00:05:41.091 --> 00:05:43.824
But in the meantime, we got
a lot of work to do, dean,

00:05:43.857 --> 00:05:45.058
And you know that.

00:05:45.091 --> 00:05:46.757
Yeah, you're right.

00:05:46.791 --> 00:05:48.991
What else you got?

00:05:49.024 --> 00:05:50.257
Uh, man in colorado.

00:05:50.290 --> 00:05:52.624
Local man by the name of daniel elkins

00:05:52.657 --> 00:05:54.524
Was found mauled in his home.

00:05:54.557 --> 00:05:57.091
Elkins. I know that name.

00:05:57.124 --> 00:05:59.091
Doesn't ring a bell.

00:05:59.124 --> 00:06:01.124
Looks like the cops
don't know what to think.

00:06:01.158 --> 00:06:04.490
At first they said it was
some sort of bear attack,

00:06:04.524 --> 00:06:06.824
And now they found signs of robbery.

00:06:06.857 --> 00:06:08.223
Mm-Hmm.

00:06:08.257 --> 00:06:10.424
Yeah.

00:06:13.924 --> 00:06:15.891
Here. Check it out.

00:06:21.724 --> 00:06:23.557
You think it's the same elkins?

00:06:23.590 --> 00:06:25.891
It's a colorado area code.

00:07:03.924 --> 00:07:06.490
Looks like the maid didn't come today.

00:07:12.257 --> 00:07:14.724
Hey, there's salt over
here, right inside the door.

00:07:14.757 --> 00:07:16.991
You mean, like,
protection-Against-Demon salt

00:07:17.024 --> 00:07:18.957
Or "oops, i spilled the popcorn" salt?

00:07:18.991 --> 00:07:20.691
It's clearly a ring.

00:07:25.158 --> 00:07:28.357
You think this guy elkins was a player?

00:07:28.390 --> 00:07:29.457
Definitely.

00:07:38.924 --> 00:07:41.390
That looks a hell of a lot like dad's.

00:07:41.424 --> 00:07:44.857
Except this dates back to the '60s.

00:08:09.791 --> 00:08:12.924
Whatever attacked him, looks
like there was more than one.

00:08:12.957 --> 00:08:15.557
Looks like he put up
a hell of a fight, too.

00:08:15.590 --> 00:08:17.957
Yeah.

00:08:44.357 --> 00:08:46.590
Got something?

00:08:48.257 --> 00:08:51.257
I don't know. Some
scratches in the floor.

00:08:51.290 --> 00:08:52.590
Death throes maybe?

00:08:52.624 --> 00:08:54.457
Maybe.

00:09:13.624 --> 00:09:15.357
Or maybe a message.

00:09:18.124 --> 00:09:21.490
Look familiar?

00:09:21.524 --> 00:09:23.757
Three letters, six digits -

00:09:23.791 --> 00:09:27.791
The location and combination
of a post office box.

00:09:27.824 --> 00:09:29.124
It's a mail drop.

00:09:29.158 --> 00:09:31.091
That's just the way dad does it.

00:09:49.891 --> 00:09:54.024
"J.W."
- You think? John winchester?

00:09:54.058 --> 00:09:56.058
I don't know. Should we open it?

00:10:00.223 --> 00:10:02.058
Dad?

00:10:04.624 --> 00:10:06.924
Dad, what are you doing
here? Are you all right?

00:10:06.957 --> 00:10:07.991
Yeah, i'm okay.

00:10:08.024 --> 00:10:09.524
Look, i read the news about daniel.

00:10:09.557 --> 00:10:12.158
I got here as fast as i could.

00:10:13.924 --> 00:10:16.357
I saw you two up at his place.

00:10:16.390 --> 00:10:18.158
Why didn't you come in, dad?

00:10:18.190 --> 00:10:19.457
You know why.

00:10:19.490 --> 00:10:22.190
Because i had to make sure
you weren't followed...

00:10:22.223 --> 00:10:23.991
By anyone...

00:10:24.024 --> 00:10:25.691
Or anything.

00:10:25.724 --> 00:10:29.058
Nice job of covering
your tracks, by the way.

00:10:29.091 --> 00:10:31.957
Yeah, well, we learned from the best.

00:10:31.991 --> 00:10:34.957
Wait, so you came all the way
out here for this elkins guy?

00:10:34.991 --> 00:10:36.158
Yeah.

00:10:36.190 --> 00:10:40.058
He was
- He was a good man.

00:10:40.091 --> 00:10:42.524
He taught me a hell
of a lot about hunting.

00:10:42.557 --> 00:10:46.024
You never mentioned him to us.

00:10:46.058 --> 00:10:48.590
We had a -

00:10:48.624 --> 00:10:51.257
We had kind of a falling out.

00:10:51.290 --> 00:10:53.924
I hadn't seen him in years.

00:10:55.791 --> 00:10:57.991
I should look at that.

00:11:06.524 --> 00:11:10.590
"If you're reading
this, i'm already dead."

00:11:10.624 --> 00:11:12.891
That son of a bitch. What is it?

00:11:12.924 --> 00:11:15.223
He had it the whole time. Dad, what?

00:11:15.257 --> 00:11:16.757
When you searched the place,

00:11:16.791 --> 00:11:19.190
Did you see a gun, an
antique, a colt revolver?

00:11:19.223 --> 00:11:20.323
Did you see it?

00:11:20.357 --> 00:11:22.557
Uh, there was an old
case, but it was empty.

00:11:22.590 --> 00:11:24.490
They have it. You mean
whatever killed elkins?

00:11:24.524 --> 00:11:26.390
We got to pick up their trail.

00:11:27.924 --> 00:11:30.891
Wait. You want us to come with you?

00:11:30.924 --> 00:11:33.257
If elkins is telling the truth,
we've got to find this gun.

00:11:33.290 --> 00:11:35.757
The gun? Why? Because
it's important, that's why.

00:11:35.791 --> 00:11:38.058
Dad, we don't even know
what these things are yet.

00:11:38.091 --> 00:11:40.091
They were what danny
elkins killed best...

00:11:40.124 --> 00:11:42.257
Vampires.

00:11:42.290 --> 00:11:43.290
Vampires?

00:11:43.323 --> 00:11:45.190
I thought there was no such thing.

00:11:45.223 --> 00:11:47.457
You never even mentioned them, dad.

00:11:47.490 --> 00:11:49.857
I thought they were extinct.

00:11:49.891 --> 00:11:53.924
I thought elkins and
others had wiped them out.

00:11:57.290 --> 00:11:58.657
I was wrong.

00:12:00.657 --> 00:12:04.024
John: most vampire lore is
crap. A cross won't repel them.

00:12:04.058 --> 00:12:05.490
Sunlight won't kill them

00:12:05.524 --> 00:12:07.857
And neither will a stake to the heart.

00:12:07.891 --> 00:12:10.124
But the bloodlust
- That part's true.

00:12:10.158 --> 00:12:12.457
They need fresh human blood to survive.

00:12:12.490 --> 00:12:13.891
They were once people,

00:12:13.924 --> 00:12:17.158
So you won't know it's a
vampire until it's too late.

00:12:17.190 --> 00:12:18.924
All yours, baby.

00:12:25.257 --> 00:12:27.390
What?

00:12:27.424 --> 00:12:29.190
Well, i guess you showed that guy.

00:12:29.223 --> 00:12:31.991
What guy? The guy who bet you
you wouldn't buy that shirt.

00:12:32.024 --> 00:12:34.223
I love this shirt.

00:12:36.891 --> 00:12:38.323
Look out!

00:12:42.691 --> 00:12:44.390
What happened to him?

00:12:44.424 --> 00:12:46.190
Call 911.

00:13:09.954 --> 00:13:12.520
Man: 22, i'm going out there.

00:13:12.554 --> 00:13:14.354
Man #2: copy that.

00:13:19.821 --> 00:13:23.153
Sam, dean, let's go.

00:13:23.187 --> 00:13:24.487
Picked up a police call.

00:13:24.520 --> 00:13:25.687
What happened?

00:13:25.721 --> 00:13:28.187
A couple called 911. They
found a body in the street.

00:13:28.220 --> 00:13:30.021
Cops got there. Everyone was missing.

00:13:30.054 --> 00:13:31.253
It's the vampires.

00:13:31.287 --> 00:13:32.687
How do you know?

00:13:32.721 --> 00:13:34.554
Just follow me, okay?

00:13:36.954 --> 00:13:38.687
Vampires.

00:13:38.721 --> 00:13:41.021
It's funny every time i hear it.

00:13:41.054 --> 00:13:43.220
[ Indistinct chatter on police radio ]

00:13:47.187 --> 00:13:49.587
I don't see why we couldn't
have gone over with him.

00:13:49.621 --> 00:13:51.554
Oh, don't tell me it's already starting.

00:13:51.587 --> 00:13:53.687
What's starting?

00:13:53.721 --> 00:13:55.454
What do you got? It was them all right.

00:13:55.487 --> 00:13:57.088
It looks like they're heading west.

00:13:57.120 --> 00:13:59.220
We have to double back
to get around that detour.

00:13:59.253 --> 00:14:00.621
How can you be so sure?

00:14:00.654 --> 00:14:02.587
I just want to know we're
going in the right direction.

00:14:02.621 --> 00:14:04.253
We are.

00:14:04.287 --> 00:14:06.187
How do you know?

00:14:06.220 --> 00:14:08.253
I found this.

00:14:10.420 --> 00:14:13.554
What is it? A vampire fang?

00:14:13.587 --> 00:14:16.721
No fangs
- Teeth. The second set descends when they attack.

00:14:16.754 --> 00:14:18.420
Any more questions?

00:14:21.654 --> 00:14:23.921
Let's get out of here.
We're losing daylight.

00:14:23.954 --> 00:14:27.721
And, dean, why don't you touch
up your car before you get rust?

00:14:27.754 --> 00:14:29.621
I wouldn't have given you the damn thing

00:14:29.654 --> 00:14:32.253
If i thought you were gonna ruin it.

00:14:39.487 --> 00:14:41.487
Vampires nest in groups of 8 to 10.

00:14:41.520 --> 00:14:43.921
Smaller packs are sent
out to hunt for food.

00:14:43.954 --> 00:14:47.187
Victims are taken to the nest,
where the pack keeps them alive,

00:14:47.220 --> 00:14:49.088
Bleeding them for days or weeks.

00:14:49.120 --> 00:14:51.787
I wonder if that's what
happened to that 911 couple.

00:14:51.821 --> 00:14:53.787
That's probably what dad's thinking.

00:14:53.821 --> 00:14:58.420
Of course, it would be nice if
he just told us what he thinks.

00:14:58.454 --> 00:15:00.287
<i>So it is starting.</i>

00:15:00.320 --> 00:15:03.021
What?

00:15:03.054 --> 00:15:04.921
Sam, we've been looking
for dad all year.

00:15:04.954 --> 00:15:07.287
Now we're not with him for
more than a couple of hours

00:15:07.320 --> 00:15:08.487
And there's static already.

00:15:08.520 --> 00:15:11.253
No.

00:15:11.287 --> 00:15:13.520
Look, i'm happy he's okay, all right,

00:15:13.554 --> 00:15:15.420
And i'm happy that we're
all working together.

00:15:15.454 --> 00:15:17.320
Good.

00:15:17.354 --> 00:15:21.520
It's just the way he treats
us like we're children.

00:15:21.554 --> 00:15:22.988
He barks orders at us, dean.

00:15:23.021 --> 00:15:25.354
He expects us to follow
him without question.

00:15:25.387 --> 00:15:27.687
He keeps us on some
crap need-To-Know deal.

00:15:27.721 --> 00:15:29.654
He does what he does for
a reason. What reason?

00:15:29.687 --> 00:15:30.887
Our job!

00:15:30.921 --> 00:15:32.721
There's no time to argue.
There's no margin for error.

00:15:32.754 --> 00:15:34.220
It's just the way the
old man runs things.

00:15:34.253 --> 00:15:36.120
Yeah, well, maybe that
worked when we were kids,

00:15:36.153 --> 00:15:37.487
But not anymore, all right?

00:15:37.520 --> 00:15:39.721
Not after everything you and
i have been through, dean.

00:15:39.754 --> 00:15:42.187
Are you telling me you're cool
with just falling into line

00:15:42.220 --> 00:15:43.854
And letting him run the whole show?

00:15:45.420 --> 00:15:49.088
If that's what it takes.

00:16:13.220 --> 00:16:15.320
Have some beer, buddy.

00:16:15.354 --> 00:16:17.554
It'll calm your nerves.

00:16:17.587 --> 00:16:19.021
No, thanks.

00:16:19.054 --> 00:16:20.320
Oh, come on.

00:16:20.354 --> 00:16:22.787
You drink enough, i can
taste it in your blood.

00:16:22.821 --> 00:16:24.520
That's gross.

00:16:32.320 --> 00:16:34.021
Well, how about you, babe?

00:16:42.287 --> 00:16:43.520
Attagirl.

00:16:50.153 --> 00:16:52.387
Bo! Wait for luther.

00:17:14.487 --> 00:17:17.220
I missed you, too, baby.

00:17:17.253 --> 00:17:19.854
We've got presents.

00:17:26.287 --> 00:17:27.721
She looks interesting.

00:17:29.787 --> 00:17:30.787
Hmm.

00:17:33.420 --> 00:17:34.654
He doesn't.

00:17:34.687 --> 00:17:36.021
Lock him up.

00:17:38.887 --> 00:17:41.921
On second thought, go
ahead and treat yourself.

00:17:46.988 --> 00:17:50.487
[ Crying ] no!

00:17:50.520 --> 00:17:52.054
There's something else.

00:17:54.021 --> 00:17:55.454
This all theirs?

00:17:55.487 --> 00:17:58.854
No. It's from an old friend of yours...

00:17:58.887 --> 00:18:00.387
Daniel elkins.

00:18:00.420 --> 00:18:02.354
I caught his scent.

00:18:02.387 --> 00:18:04.887
I thought i'd surprise you.

00:18:04.921 --> 00:18:06.787
Kate, what did you do?

00:18:06.821 --> 00:18:08.520
I made him suffer.

00:18:08.554 --> 00:18:10.621
You shouldn't have done that.

00:18:10.654 --> 00:18:12.021
There are others like him.

00:18:12.054 --> 00:18:14.054
They'll know the signs
and come looking for us.

00:18:14.088 --> 00:18:15.153
We have to be careful.

00:18:15.187 --> 00:18:16.454
Luther, i did it for you,

00:18:16.487 --> 00:18:17.988
For what he did to your family.

00:18:18.021 --> 00:18:20.021
Revenge isn't worth
much if you end up dead.

00:18:23.220 --> 00:18:24.887
I'm sorry, babe.

00:18:24.921 --> 00:18:27.253
I'm sorry.

00:18:33.153 --> 00:18:35.153
I thought you might like that.

00:18:35.187 --> 00:18:37.921
Looks like it was made
around the time you were born.

00:18:39.954 --> 00:18:41.821
I've seen this before.

00:18:41.854 --> 00:18:44.387
Elkins died with it in his hands.

00:18:44.420 --> 00:18:48.320
He should have known better
- Using a gun.

00:18:48.354 --> 00:18:51.721
This is no ordinary gun.

00:18:51.754 --> 00:18:53.887
Yeah, dad. All right, got it.

00:18:53.921 --> 00:18:55.988
Pull off the next exit. Why?

00:18:56.021 --> 00:18:58.054
'Cause dad thinks we
got the vampires' trail.

00:18:58.088 --> 00:18:59.120
How?

00:18:59.153 --> 00:19:01.354
I don't know. He didn't say.

00:19:12.854 --> 00:19:15.420
Oh, crap. Here we go.

00:19:15.454 --> 00:19:17.287
What the hell was that? We need to talk.

00:19:17.320 --> 00:19:18.754
About what? About everything.

00:19:18.787 --> 00:19:21.287
Where we going, dad? What's
the big deal about this gun?

00:19:21.320 --> 00:19:23.387
We can q&a after we
kill all the vampires.

00:19:23.420 --> 00:19:25.654
Your brother's right. We
don't have time for this.

00:19:25.687 --> 00:19:28.054
Last we saw you, you said it
was too dangerous to be together.

00:19:28.088 --> 00:19:29.687
Now, out of the blue, you need our help.

00:19:29.721 --> 00:19:32.120
Obviously something big's going
down, and we want to know what!

00:19:32.153 --> 00:19:34.253
Get back in the car. No.

00:19:34.287 --> 00:19:36.520
I said get back in the damn car.

00:19:36.554 --> 00:19:37.921
Yeah, and i said no.

00:19:37.954 --> 00:19:39.621
All right, you made
your point, tough guy.

00:19:39.654 --> 00:19:41.887
Look, we're all tired. We
can talk about this later.

00:19:41.921 --> 00:19:43.187
Sammy, i mean it. Come on.

00:19:43.220 --> 00:19:44.854
This is why i left in the first place.

00:19:44.887 --> 00:19:46.754
What'd you say? You heard me.

00:19:46.787 --> 00:19:47.821
<i>Yeah, you left.</i>

00:19:47.854 --> 00:19:50.287
Your brother and me
- We needed you.

00:19:50.320 --> 00:19:52.854
You walked away, sam. You walked away!

00:19:52.887 --> 00:19:55.320
You're the one who said,
"don't come back," dad.

00:19:55.354 --> 00:19:57.621
You're the one who
closed that door, not me!

00:19:57.654 --> 00:20:00.420
You were just pissed off you
couldn't control me anymore!

00:20:00.454 --> 00:20:02.153
Stop it! Stop it! Stop it!

00:20:02.187 --> 00:20:04.187
That's enough!

00:20:05.687 --> 00:20:07.287
That means you, too.

00:20:15.120 --> 00:20:16.687
Terrific.

00:20:39.954 --> 00:20:42.021
Luther: you like to watch, huh?

00:20:42.054 --> 00:20:44.220
Me too.

00:20:46.487 --> 00:20:48.153
Ready, baby?

00:21:02.520 --> 00:21:05.721
Are you gonna kill me?

00:21:05.754 --> 00:21:10.187
I'm gonna take you so high
you're never gonna come down.

00:21:48.120 --> 00:21:50.487
Welcome home, baby.

00:22:07.827 --> 00:22:09.427
I know what time it is.

00:22:09.460 --> 00:22:10.927
Get in.

00:22:14.261 --> 00:22:17.328
Dean: son of a bitch.

00:22:17.360 --> 00:22:19.827
So they're really not afraid of the sun?

00:22:19.861 --> 00:22:22.694
No, direct sunlight hurts
like a nasty sunburn.

00:22:22.727 --> 00:22:26.594
The only way to kill
them is by beheading.

00:22:26.627 --> 00:22:30.061
And, yeah, they sleep during the day.

00:22:30.094 --> 00:22:33.493
It doesn't mean they won't wake up.

00:22:33.527 --> 00:22:36.994
So i guess walking right
in's not our best option.

00:22:37.027 --> 00:22:39.894
Actually, that's the plan.

00:22:47.927 --> 00:22:49.527
Dad, i've got an extra
machete if you need one.

00:22:49.560 --> 00:22:53.061
Think i'm okay. Thanks.

00:22:53.094 --> 00:22:55.027
Wow.

00:23:01.694 --> 00:23:04.460
So...

00:23:04.493 --> 00:23:07.161
You boys really want
to know about this colt?

00:23:11.261 --> 00:23:12.794
Yes, sir.

00:23:12.827 --> 00:23:15.261
It's just a story...

00:23:15.294 --> 00:23:18.261
A legend, really.

00:23:18.294 --> 00:23:20.393
Well, i thought it was.

00:23:20.427 --> 00:23:23.393
Never really believed it
until i read daniel's letter.

00:23:23.427 --> 00:23:27.294
Back in 1835, when
halley's comet was overhead,

00:23:27.328 --> 00:23:30.927
The same night those
men died at the alamo,

00:23:30.961 --> 00:23:33.861
They say samuel colt made a gun...

00:23:33.894 --> 00:23:35.161
A special gun.

00:23:35.194 --> 00:23:37.261
He made it for a hunter -

00:23:37.294 --> 00:23:40.660
A man like us, only on horseback.

00:23:40.694 --> 00:23:43.627
The story goes he made 13 bullets.

00:23:43.660 --> 00:23:47.594
This hunter used the
gun a half dozen times

00:23:47.627 --> 00:23:51.927
Before he disappeared,
the gun along with him.

00:23:51.961 --> 00:23:55.427
Somehow, daniel got his hands on it.

00:23:55.460 --> 00:23:57.760
They say -

00:23:57.794 --> 00:24:00.427
They say this gun can kill anything.

00:24:00.460 --> 00:24:03.894
Kill anything, like
supernatural anything?

00:24:05.127 --> 00:24:06.894
Like the demon.

00:24:06.927 --> 00:24:08.760
Yeah, the demon.

00:24:08.794 --> 00:24:11.660
Ever since i picked up its trail,

00:24:11.694 --> 00:24:15.861
I've been looking for a
way to destroy that thing.

00:24:15.894 --> 00:24:19.794
Find the gun...

00:24:19.827 --> 00:24:22.328
We may have it.

00:25:53.994 --> 00:25:55.927
Sam: dean.

00:26:19.861 --> 00:26:21.660
There's more.

00:26:56.627 --> 00:26:59.161
Hey.

00:26:59.194 --> 00:27:01.261
Hey, hey, shh. I'm here to help you.

00:27:13.827 --> 00:27:15.493
John: boys, run!

00:27:16.393 --> 00:27:17.594
Dad!

00:27:25.861 --> 00:27:27.427
Dad?!

00:27:29.760 --> 00:27:31.493
Dad?!

00:27:36.727 --> 00:27:39.027
They won't follow. They'll till tonight.

00:27:39.061 --> 00:27:41.460
Once a vampire gets your
scent, it's for life.

00:27:41.493 --> 00:27:42.694
What do we do now?

00:27:42.727 --> 00:27:44.794
You got to find the
nearest funeral home.

00:27:47.560 --> 00:27:49.961
It shouldn't be taking this long.

00:27:49.994 --> 00:27:52.427
I should go help.

00:27:52.460 --> 00:27:54.827
Dean's got it.

00:28:02.360 --> 00:28:04.194
Sammy.

00:28:05.861 --> 00:28:06.861
Yeah?

00:28:09.794 --> 00:28:12.328
I don't think i ever told you this,

00:28:12.360 --> 00:28:15.594
But the day you were
born, you know what i did?

00:28:15.627 --> 00:28:17.694
No.

00:28:17.727 --> 00:28:20.794
I put 100 bucks into a
savings account for you.

00:28:20.827 --> 00:28:23.427
I did the same thing for your brother.

00:28:26.194 --> 00:28:27.727
It was a college fund.

00:28:30.061 --> 00:28:35.228
And every month, i'd put
in another $100 until...

00:28:37.261 --> 00:28:39.660
Anyway, my point is, sam, that

00:28:41.660 --> 00:28:43.794
This is never the life
that i wanted for you.

00:28:43.827 --> 00:28:46.527
Then why'd you get so mad when i left?

00:28:46.560 --> 00:28:50.061
You got to understand something.

00:28:50.094 --> 00:28:52.660
After your mother passed,

00:28:52.694 --> 00:28:56.527
All i saw was evil, everywhere.

00:28:56.560 --> 00:29:02.094
And all i cared about was
keeping you boys alive.

00:29:02.127 --> 00:29:05.594
I wanted you prepared...

00:29:05.627 --> 00:29:07.127
Ready.

00:29:09.360 --> 00:29:11.961
So somewhere along the line, i, uh

00:29:14.660 --> 00:29:16.660
I stopped being your father.

00:29:16.694 --> 00:29:18.560
And i -

00:29:18.594 --> 00:29:22.261
I became your drill sergeant.

00:29:24.294 --> 00:29:28.094
So when you said you
wanted to go away to school,

00:29:28.127 --> 00:29:31.393
All i could think
about, my only thought,

00:29:31.427 --> 00:29:36.460
Was that you were gonna be alone...

00:29:36.493 --> 00:29:38.427
Vulnerable.

00:29:38.460 --> 00:29:41.261
Sammy, it just -

00:29:41.294 --> 00:29:43.427
It never occurred to me what you wanted.

00:29:45.294 --> 00:29:47.594
I just couldn't accept the fact

00:29:47.627 --> 00:29:50.393
That you and me...

00:29:50.427 --> 00:29:51.594
We're just different.

00:29:53.194 --> 00:29:54.460
What?

00:29:57.727 --> 00:29:59.294
We're not different.

00:30:01.727 --> 00:30:03.861
Not anymore.

00:30:06.660 --> 00:30:09.360
With what happened to mom and jess

00:30:13.127 --> 00:30:15.194
We probably have a lot more in common

00:30:15.228 --> 00:30:17.927
Than just about anyone.

00:30:20.294 --> 00:30:22.660
I guess you're right, son.

00:30:26.393 --> 00:30:28.560
Hey, dad?

00:30:30.760 --> 00:30:32.760
Whatever happened to that college fund?

00:30:34.727 --> 00:30:36.527
Spent it on ammo.

00:30:43.594 --> 00:30:44.961
Whoo!

00:30:44.994 --> 00:30:48.493
Man, there's some heavy security
to protect a bunch of dead guys.

00:30:48.527 --> 00:30:50.694
Did you get it?

00:31:00.161 --> 00:31:03.061
You know what to do.

00:31:11.961 --> 00:31:13.627
Kate: car trouble?

00:31:17.794 --> 00:31:19.994
Let me give you a lift...

00:31:20.027 --> 00:31:21.927
Take you back to my place.

00:31:21.961 --> 00:31:23.061
I'll pass.

00:31:23.094 --> 00:31:25.427
I usually draw the line at necrophilia.

00:31:39.727 --> 00:31:43.360
I don't normally get this
friendly till the second date.

00:31:43.393 --> 00:31:46.427
You know, we could have some fun.

00:31:46.460 --> 00:31:49.627
I always like to make new friends.

00:31:59.527 --> 00:32:02.393
Oh, sorry.

00:32:02.427 --> 00:32:04.827
I never really stay
with a chick that long.

00:32:04.861 --> 00:32:06.161
Definitely not eternity.

00:32:06.194 --> 00:32:07.427
Ugh!

00:32:11.861 --> 00:32:13.861
Damn it.

00:32:15.360 --> 00:32:17.194
Barely even stings.

00:32:17.228 --> 00:32:19.560
Give it time, sweetheart.

00:32:19.594 --> 00:32:21.827
That arrow's soaked in dead man's blood.

00:32:21.861 --> 00:32:24.294
It's like poison to you, isn't it?

00:32:27.560 --> 00:32:28.861
Load her up.

00:32:28.894 --> 00:32:31.294
I'll take care of this one.

00:32:41.951 --> 00:32:43.250
Toss this on the fire.

00:32:43.284 --> 00:32:45.384
Saffron, skunks,
cabbage, and trillium -

00:32:45.417 --> 00:32:47.984
It'll block our scent and
hers until we're ready.

00:32:48.018 --> 00:32:49.817
Stuff stinks. Well, that's the idea.

00:32:49.851 --> 00:32:51.517
Dust your clothes with the ashes

00:32:51.551 --> 00:32:53.817
And you'll stand a chance
of not being detected.

00:32:53.851 --> 00:32:55.484
You sure they'll come after her?

00:32:55.517 --> 00:32:57.651
Yeah. Vampires mate for life.

00:32:57.684 --> 00:33:00.150
She means more to the
leader than the gun.

00:33:00.183 --> 00:33:02.117
But the blood sickness
is gonna wear off soon,

00:33:02.150 --> 00:33:03.584
So you don't have a lot of time.

00:33:03.617 --> 00:33:05.083
Half-Hour ought to do it.

00:33:05.117 --> 00:33:07.884
And then i want you out of
the area as fast as you can.

00:33:07.918 --> 00:33:09.117
But -

00:33:09.150 --> 00:33:10.717
You can't take care
of them all yourself.

00:33:10.751 --> 00:33:13.083
I'll have her and the colt.

00:33:13.117 --> 00:33:16.617
But after, we're gonna meet up, right?

00:33:16.651 --> 00:33:20.250
Use the gun together, right?

00:33:22.150 --> 00:33:24.517
You're leaving again, aren't you?

00:33:26.684 --> 00:33:30.150
You still want to go
after the demon alone?

00:33:30.183 --> 00:33:31.651
You know, i don't get you.

00:33:31.684 --> 00:33:34.250
You can't treat us like this. Like what?

00:33:34.284 --> 00:33:35.450
Like children.

00:33:35.484 --> 00:33:38.617
You are my children. I'm
trying to keep you safe.

00:33:38.651 --> 00:33:41.450
Dad, all due respect, but
that's a bunch of crap.

00:33:42.384 --> 00:33:44.517
Excuse me?

00:33:44.551 --> 00:33:46.584
You know what sammy
and i have been hunting.

00:33:46.617 --> 00:33:48.884
Hell, you sent us on a
few hunting trips yourself.

00:33:48.918 --> 00:33:51.050
You can't be that worried
about keeping us safe.

00:33:51.083 --> 00:33:52.617
It's not the same thing, de.

00:33:52.651 --> 00:33:53.751
Then what is it?

00:33:53.784 --> 00:33:55.817
Why do you want us out of the big fight?

00:33:55.851 --> 00:33:57.684
This demon...

00:33:57.717 --> 00:34:00.851
It's a bad son of a bitch.

00:34:00.884 --> 00:34:02.417
I can't make the same moves

00:34:02.450 --> 00:34:04.751
If i'm worried about keeping you alive.

00:34:04.784 --> 00:34:05.951
You can't be as reckless.

00:34:05.984 --> 00:34:07.384
Look...

00:34:07.417 --> 00:34:10.984
I don't expect to make it out
of this fight in one piece.

00:34:13.183 --> 00:34:16.617
Your mother's death...

00:34:16.651 --> 00:34:18.250
It almost killed me.

00:34:19.884 --> 00:34:23.751
I can't watch my children die, too.

00:34:23.784 --> 00:34:24.918
I won't.

00:34:24.951 --> 00:34:26.984
What happens if you die?

00:34:27.018 --> 00:34:28.984
Dad, what happens if you die

00:34:29.018 --> 00:34:31.484
And we could have done
something about it?

00:34:31.517 --> 00:34:32.751
You know, i've been thinking.

00:34:32.784 --> 00:34:34.651
I think maybe sammy's
right about this one.

00:34:34.684 --> 00:34:36.317
I think we should do this together.

00:34:38.584 --> 00:34:41.183
We're stronger as a family,
dad. We just are. You know it.

00:34:42.651 --> 00:34:44.250
We're running out of time.

00:34:45.684 --> 00:34:48.350
You do your job, and
you get out of the area.

00:34:49.584 --> 00:34:51.517
That's an order.

00:35:01.484 --> 00:35:03.684
Is there any sign of those three?

00:35:03.717 --> 00:35:05.651
No. Something else.

00:35:05.684 --> 00:35:07.751
What? Luther, they cut off hank's head.

00:35:07.784 --> 00:35:09.851
And kate?

00:35:09.884 --> 00:35:12.884
I don't know. She wasn't there.

00:35:14.350 --> 00:35:16.018
What are we gonna do?

00:35:21.317 --> 00:35:23.884
It's just a truck up on the highway.

00:35:28.984 --> 00:35:31.417
Kate.

00:35:31.450 --> 00:35:33.717
She's in that truck.

00:36:33.851 --> 00:36:35.284
Boo.

00:36:51.450 --> 00:36:53.684
I told you i'd come back.

00:37:12.450 --> 00:37:14.551
Luther: get out!

00:37:18.784 --> 00:37:20.018
Who are you?

00:37:20.050 --> 00:37:21.384
The name's winchester.

00:37:21.417 --> 00:37:22.851
Where are your friends?

00:37:22.884 --> 00:37:24.450
Cleaning out your nest.

00:37:26.784 --> 00:37:28.484
Where's kate?

00:37:28.517 --> 00:37:30.651
Come here, sweetheart.

00:37:38.250 --> 00:37:40.183
Kate, you all right?

00:37:42.083 --> 00:37:44.317
Dead man's blood.

00:37:44.350 --> 00:37:46.384
You son of a bitch.

00:37:46.417 --> 00:37:50.083
I want the colt
- Elkins' gun.

00:37:50.117 --> 00:37:51.117
Trade.

00:37:51.150 --> 00:37:52.517
Is that what this is all about?

00:37:52.551 --> 00:37:54.350
I mean, you can't shoot us all, right?

00:37:54.384 --> 00:37:55.817
We'll kill you.

00:37:55.851 --> 00:37:58.484
Oh, i don't need it for you.

00:37:58.517 --> 00:38:01.484
I'm saving it for something else.

00:38:01.517 --> 00:38:05.083
Now, put the colt
down or she goes first.

00:38:05.117 --> 00:38:07.717
All right.

00:38:07.751 --> 00:38:10.018
Just don't hurt her.

00:38:17.350 --> 00:38:18.617
Back up.

00:38:20.784 --> 00:38:22.150
Further.

00:38:34.050 --> 00:38:36.551
That's a nice move. You almost made it.

00:39:01.150 --> 00:39:02.183
Ugh!

00:39:06.651 --> 00:39:09.150
Don't! I'll break his neck.

00:39:09.183 --> 00:39:10.851
Put the blade down.

00:39:24.117 --> 00:39:26.717
You people.

00:39:26.751 --> 00:39:28.751
Why can't you just leave us alone?

00:39:28.784 --> 00:39:31.083
We have as much right to live as you do.

00:39:31.117 --> 00:39:32.651
John: i don't think so.

00:39:59.217 --> 00:40:01.884
Luther!

00:40:17.018 --> 00:40:19.117
Kate, don't!

00:40:42.984 --> 00:40:44.984
So, boys...

00:40:49.283 --> 00:40:50.951
Yes, sir?

00:40:50.984 --> 00:40:53.517
You ignored a direct order back there.

00:40:53.550 --> 00:40:55.917
Yes, sir. But we saved your ass.

00:41:01.218 --> 00:41:02.617
You're right.

00:41:02.650 --> 00:41:04.951
I am?

00:41:04.984 --> 00:41:07.350
It scares the hell out of me.

00:41:07.383 --> 00:41:09.250
You two are all i've got.

00:41:11.151 --> 00:41:14.884
But i guess we are stronger as a family.

00:41:14.917 --> 00:41:17.584
So...

00:41:17.617 --> 00:41:21.283
We go after this damn thing...

00:41:21.317 --> 00:41:23.250
Together.

00:41:23.283 --> 00:41:25.517
Yes, sir.Yes, sir.



00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:22.000
